## Start here: `dude cheatsheet`

Before reading further, run:

```bash
dude cheatsheet --format json
```

One call returns **this project's** live command catalog, every lint rule with its
code and title, the verify loop, and the answers it was scaffolded with. It is
generated from the project itself, so it cannot drift from reality the way a
hand-written list can — prefer it over any command list in this file.

Then verify your own work before claiming it is done:

```bash
dude lint     # structural conventions; each code has prose in .claude/rules/
dude test     # the project's test suites
```

When `dude lint` reports a code, read `.claude/rules/<GROUP>/<NNN>.md` for why the
rule exists and how to fix it properly — do not work around a diagnostic.

