## dude CLI — all available commands

Run `dude help` for the live catalog (it includes `.dude/commands/` too).

### Desktop app

| Command | Meaning |
| ------- | ------- |
| `dude dev` | Run the app in development mode (Vite + Rust hot-reload). |
| `dude build` | Build distributable installers (`--debug`, `--bundles <list>`, `--target <triple>`). |
| `dude doctor` | Verify Node, Rust and platform prerequisites (desktop + mobile). |
| `dude icon` | Regenerate `src-tauri/icons/` from `app-icon.png` (`--source <png>`). |

> Installers from `dude build` are **ad-hoc signed** by default: they run on
> the build machine but show *"damaged"* (macOS) or a SmartScreen warning
> (Windows) elsewhere. To distribute, configure Developer ID signing +
> notarization — see `docs/docs/distribute.md`.

### Mobile app (same codebase — see docs/docs/mobile.md)

| Command | Meaning |
| ------- | ------- |
| `dude android init` | One-time: install Rust targets + generate `src-tauri/gen/android`. |
| `dude android dev` | Run on emulator/device (`--open` for Android Studio, `--host` for physical devices). |
| `dude android build` | Build APK/AAB (`--debug`, `--apk`, `--aab`, `--target <abis>`). |
| `dude ios init` | One-time (macOS): install Rust targets + generate `src-tauri/gen/apple`. |
| `dude ios dev` | Run on simulator/device (`--open` for Xcode, `--host` for physical devices). |
| `dude ios build` | Build the IPA (`--debug`, `--export-method <m>`). |

### Code quality

| Command | Meaning |
| ------- | ------- |
| `dude lint` | Structural checks — FE (React) + BE (Rust/Tauri). Exit 1 on errors. |
| `dude format` | prettier (frontend) + cargo fmt (backend). `--check` to verify only. |
| `dude review` | lint + ESLint + tsc + cargo fmt --check + cargo clippy. |
| `dude test` | cargo test (`--filter <substr>` to narrow). |

### Documentation

| Command | Meaning |
| ------- | ------- |
| `dude docs` | Serve MkDocs at http://localhost:8001 (requires Docker; `--port <n>`). |

