## Core Tauri concepts (as wired in this project)

1. **Commands** — Rust functions annotated `#[tauri::command]` in
   `src-tauri/src/commands/<domain>.rs`, registered in `generate_handler![…]`
   in `lib.rs`, and called from the frontend **only** through the matching
   typed wrapper in `src/ipc/<domain>.ts`.
2. **Managed state** — `AppState` (`state.rs`) registered with `app.manage()`;
   commands receive `tauri::State<'_, AppState>`. Interior mutability via
   `Mutex`. Never global statics.
3. **Events** — the backend broadcasts with `app.emit(EVENT, payload)`; the
   frontend subscribes with the `useTauriEvent` hook. Event names live as
   constants in the `src/ipc/` module of the domain that emits them.
4. **Errors** — every fallible command returns `Result<_, AppError>`
   (`error.rs`); the frontend receives the serialized message as the promise
   rejection.
5. **Capabilities** — permissions per window in `src-tauri/capabilities/`;
   grant the minimum each window needs.
{{#if withSqlite}}
6. **Persistence** — `db.rs` opens SQLite in the app-data dir and applies
   append-only migrations at startup; command modules keep query logic in
   plain functions over `&Connection` so tests run in-memory.
{{/if}}

The Home page (`src/pages/Home/`) is a live demo of 1–4: read it first.

## Adding a feature end-to-end

1. Rust: add `src-tauri/src/commands/<domain>.rs` (logic in plain functions +
   thin `#[tauri::command]` bindings + `#[cfg(test)]` tests).
2. Declare it in `commands/mod.rs`; register each command in
   `generate_handler![…]` in `lib.rs`.
3. Frontend: add the typed wrapper `src/ipc/<domain>.ts` and its barrel export
   in `src/ipc/index.ts`.
4. UI: add `src/pages/<Name>/index.tsx`, route it in `App.tsx`, add the menu
   entry in `components/Layout/`.
5. Validate: `dude lint && dude test && dude review`.

