## Conventions Claude must follow

- **Frontend**: strict TypeScript; antd components; pages/components/hooks
  layout and barrels per `.claude/rules/FE/`; never call `invoke()` outside
  `src/ipc/`; never import `@tauri-apps/api/event` outside `src/hooks/`.
- **Backend**: rules in `.claude/rules/BE/` — thin `main.rs`, commands only
  under `commands/`, `AppError` everywhere, no `unwrap`/`expect` in commands,
  `log::…` instead of `println!`, minimal capabilities, unit tests per module.
- **Always run `dude lint` after structural changes** — it enforces all of the
  above and the rule files explain every violation.
- Use `pnpm`, not `npm`/`yarn`.

## What Claude should NOT do

- Do not edit `dude.json` (use `dude upgrade`).
- Do not edit `src-tauri/target/`, `src-tauri/gen/schemas/`, `dist/`
  (generated). `src-tauri/gen/android` and `src-tauri/gen/apple` are the
  exception: they are scaffolded once by `dude android|ios init`, committed,
  and edited deliberately for native customisation (manifests, signing).
- Do not weaken `tauri.conf.json` security (CSP) or widen capabilities beyond
  what a feature strictly needs.
- Do not remove the `mobile_entry_point` attribute from `lib.rs` or change
  `[lib] crate-type` in `Cargo.toml` — mobile builds depend on both (BE012).
- Do not commit anything under `private/`.

